17.60.340.m:
The press-cakes are accompanied by calls;
"Recite," "Sacrifice" are [the calls] for that to Anīkavat.
The oblation to the Sāṃtapanas follows after the midday press-cakes.

17.61.341.m:
Then in the morning [there is] threefold sacrificial grass;
he strews it as a single layer.
Then he dedicates the animal to Agni.
